### Sample requests — open in IntelliJ (HTTP Client) and click ▶ next to each request.
### Start the app first (dev profile seeds 3 leave requests with ids 1-3).

### 1. Get all leave requests
GET http://localhost:8080/leaves

### 2. Filter by employee and status
GET http://localhost:8080/leaves?employeeId=EMP001&status=PENDING

### 3. Get one leave request
GET http://localhost:8080/leaves/1

### 4. Create a leave request (201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP010",
  "leaveType": "CASUAL",
  "startDate": "2026-12-21",
  "endDate": "2026-12-23",
  "reason": "Attending sister's wedding"
}

### 5. Update (approve) a leave request (200 OK)
PUT http://localhost:8080/leaves/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP001",
  "leaveType": "CASUAL",
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-02",
  "reason": "Family function in hometown",
  "status": "APPROVED"
}

### 6. Delete a leave request (204 No Content)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/leaves/3

### --- Error scenarios ---

### 7. Not found (404)
GET http://localhost:8080/leaves/999

### 8. Validation errors (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "",
  "leaveType": "CASUAL",
  "startDate": "2026-12-10",
  "endDate": "2026-12-05",
  "reason": "abc"
}

### 9. Unknown leave type (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/leaves
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP010",
  "leaveType": "VACATION",
  "startDate": "2026-12-10",
  "endDate": "2026-12-11",
  "reason": "Trip with friends"
}

### 10. Updating a finalized leave (409) — run after request 5
PUT http://localhost:8080/leaves/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "EMP001",
  "leaveType": "CASUAL",
  "startDate": "2026-12-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-02",
  "reason": "Family function in hometown",
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}
